1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,290
A lift goes up three
floors, then down three.

2
00:00:03,290 --> 00:00:05,705
A swimmer swims one length, then back.

3
00:00:06,105 --> 00:00:09,438
Each one travels, and ends
exactly where it started.

4
00:00:09,438 --> 00:00:11,558
So how far has it really moved?

5
00:00:12,008 --> 00:00:16,397
Aarav rides from his home to the shop,
two hundred metres down the road.

6
00:00:16,397 --> 00:00:18,000
Then he rides back home.

7
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:21,661
His bicycle wheels have
rolled four hundred metres.

8
00:00:21,661 --> 00:00:23,679
But his displacement is zero.

9
00:00:24,079 --> 00:00:25,576
Both numbers are true.

10
00:00:25,576 --> 00:00:29,896
By the end of this video, you will
see why displacement can be zero.

11
00:00:30,546 --> 00:00:31,822
First, position.

12
00:00:31,822 --> 00:00:35,440
Last time we picked an origin
and a positive direction.

13
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:40,271
Put the origin at Aarav's home, and
call the way to the shop positive.

14
00:00:40,671 --> 00:00:45,039
Position is where something is,
measured from the origin, with a sign.

15
00:00:45,039 --> 00:00:46,349
We write it as x.

16
00:00:46,749 --> 00:00:49,402
The shop is at plus two hundred metres.

17
00:00:49,402 --> 00:00:53,283
A tea stall behind the home is
at minus one hundred metres.

18
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:56,679
Now let's run the ride
on our motion notebook.

19
00:00:57,029 --> 00:00:58,394
Aarav leaves home.

20
00:00:58,394 --> 00:00:59,811
His position grows.

21
00:00:59,811 --> 00:01:02,327
Twenty, fifty, one hundred metres.

22
00:01:02,727 --> 00:01:05,031
The violet arrow is his displacement.

23
00:01:05,031 --> 00:01:08,562
It always runs from where he
started to where he is now.

24
00:01:08,962 --> 00:01:13,437
At the shop, x is two hundred metres,
and the arrow is two hundred metres

25
00:01:13,437 --> 00:01:14,337
long.

26
00:01:14,359 --> 00:01:15,583
Now he turns back.

27
00:01:15,583 --> 00:01:18,383
His wheels keep rolling,
but the arrow shrinks.

28
00:01:18,783 --> 00:01:19,887
Slow-mo replay.

29
00:01:19,887 --> 00:01:24,511
The path counter keeps rising, but
the arrow only cares about start and

30
00:01:24,511 --> 00:01:25,411
end.

31
00:01:25,537 --> 00:01:26,874
He reaches home.

32
00:01:26,874 --> 00:01:29,275
The path is four hundred metres.

33
00:01:29,275 --> 00:01:30,785
The arrow is gone.

34
00:01:30,785 --> 00:01:32,393
Displacement is zero.

35
00:01:33,043 --> 00:01:35,382
Let's reason it out, one link at a time.

36
00:01:35,732 --> 00:01:38,019
Displacement is the change in position.

37
00:01:38,019 --> 00:01:41,645
Only two things matter: where
you start, and where you end.

38
00:01:42,045 --> 00:01:44,268
The road in between does not count.

39
00:01:44,668 --> 00:01:47,273
Aarav starts at home and ends at home.

40
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:49,571
Start and end are the same point.

41
00:01:49,571 --> 00:01:51,503
So his displacement is zero.

42
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:55,054
Now let's write it as a
rule, one step at a time.

43
00:01:55,404 --> 00:01:56,304
Step one.

44
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,750
At the start, the position is x one.

45
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:01,204
At the end, the position is x two.

46
00:02:01,954 --> 00:02:02,942
Step two.

47
00:02:02,942 --> 00:02:05,772
Displacement is final minus initial.

48
00:02:05,772 --> 00:02:08,638
Delta x equals x two minus x one.

49
00:02:09,388 --> 00:02:10,368
Step three.

50
00:02:10,368 --> 00:02:12,340
The sign is the direction.

51
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:15,025
Plus means he moved the positive way.

52
00:02:15,025 --> 00:02:17,157
Minus means the negative way.

53
00:02:17,907 --> 00:02:19,138
Check the units.

54
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:21,340
Metres minus metres gives metres.

55
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:24,834
A length with a direction:
displacement is a vector.

56
00:02:25,484 --> 00:02:26,617
Remember this.

57
00:02:26,617 --> 00:02:30,185
Displacement is final position
minus initial position.

58
00:02:30,185 --> 00:02:32,694
Only the start and the end matter.

59
00:02:33,394 --> 00:02:34,597
Side by side.

60
00:02:34,597 --> 00:02:37,514
Home to shop: two hundred minus zero.

61
00:02:37,514 --> 00:02:40,209
Delta x is plus two hundred metres.

62
00:02:40,609 --> 00:02:43,498
Shop to home: zero minus two hundred.

63
00:02:43,498 --> 00:02:46,222
Delta x is minus two hundred metres.

64
00:02:46,222 --> 00:02:48,250
Same road, opposite sign.

65
00:02:48,850 --> 00:02:49,876
Now you try.

66
00:02:49,876 --> 00:02:52,802
Aarav rides from the
shop to the tea stall.

67
00:02:52,802 --> 00:02:56,116
Plus three hundred, or
minus three hundred metres?

68
00:02:56,116 --> 00:02:57,390
Pause and decide.

69
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:01,969
Minus three hundred!

70
00:03:01,969 --> 00:03:05,922
Minus one hundred, minus two
hundred, is minus three hundred.

71
00:03:05,922 --> 00:03:07,705
He moved the negative way.

72
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:10,115
Here is a deeper question.

73
00:03:10,465 --> 00:03:12,477
Move the origin to the shop.

74
00:03:12,477 --> 00:03:15,249
Does the home to shop displacement change?

75
00:03:15,249 --> 00:03:16,530
Pause and decide.

76
00:03:19,730 --> 00:03:21,121
It does not change!

77
00:03:21,121 --> 00:03:25,013
Now home is at minus two
hundred, and the shop is at zero.

78
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:28,855
Zero minus minus two hundred
is still plus two hundred.

79
00:03:28,855 --> 00:03:33,033
Both positions shift by the same
amount, so their difference stays the

80
00:03:33,033 --> 00:03:33,933
same.

81
00:03:34,218 --> 00:03:35,954
Now, one worked example.

82
00:03:36,304 --> 00:03:40,900
In the college corridor, Aarav starts
twelve metres from the stairs, walks

83
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:45,319
to the library at forty seven metres,
then back to the water cooler at

84
00:03:45,319 --> 00:03:46,372
thirty metres.

85
00:03:46,372 --> 00:03:47,878
Find his displacement.

86
00:03:48,378 --> 00:03:49,645
Use the rule.

87
00:03:49,645 --> 00:03:52,437
Delta x equals x two minus x one.

88
00:03:53,187 --> 00:03:55,102
Only start and end matter.

89
00:03:55,102 --> 00:03:58,518
x one is twelve metres,
x two is thirty metres.

90
00:03:58,518 --> 00:04:00,547
The library is just a stop.

91
00:04:01,297 --> 00:04:03,749
So delta x is thirty minus twelve.

92
00:04:03,749 --> 00:04:05,818
That is plus eighteen metres.

93
00:04:06,568 --> 00:04:10,122
The path was thirty five
metres out and seventeen back.

94
00:04:10,122 --> 00:04:13,655
Fifty two metres walked, only
eighteen of displacement.

95
00:04:14,305 --> 00:04:15,771
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:16,121 --> 00:04:20,631
Many students take the bigger number
minus the smaller one, so displacement

97
00:04:20,631 --> 00:04:22,378
always comes out positive.

98
00:04:22,728 --> 00:04:25,644
But displacement is always
final minus initial.

99
00:04:25,644 --> 00:04:28,976
From two hundred to zero,
it is minus two hundred.

100
00:04:28,976 --> 00:04:31,119
The sign is part of the answer.

101
00:04:31,769 --> 00:04:33,151
Where is this asked?

102
00:04:33,151 --> 00:04:37,298
As short questions on displacement,
often with the path length placed in

103
00:04:37,298 --> 00:04:38,828
the options as a trap.

104
00:04:39,428 --> 00:04:40,656
Exam level now.

105
00:04:40,656 --> 00:04:45,485
The position of a particle is x equals
three t squared, minus twelve t,

106
00:04:45,485 --> 00:04:46,390
plus five.

107
00:04:46,390 --> 00:04:50,022
Find its displacement from
one second to four seconds.

108
00:04:50,022 --> 00:04:51,302
Pause and solve.

109
00:04:56,702 --> 00:04:58,067
The answer is C.

110
00:04:58,067 --> 00:04:59,422
Plus nine metres.

111
00:04:59,922 --> 00:05:04,561
At one second, x is three minus
twelve plus five, minus four metres.

112
00:05:04,561 --> 00:05:09,611
At four seconds, x is forty eight minus
forty eight plus five, five metres.

113
00:05:10,111 --> 00:05:13,740
Delta x is five minus minus
four, plus nine metres.

114
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:17,317
Fifteen is the path: it
turns back at two seconds.

115
00:05:17,917 --> 00:05:19,381
Here is your recap.

116
00:05:19,381 --> 00:05:20,885
Screenshot this card.

117
00:05:24,085 --> 00:05:27,084
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

118
00:05:27,484 --> 00:05:28,384
One.

119
00:05:27,990 --> 00:05:30,291
Aarav rides to the shop and back.

120
00:05:30,291 --> 00:05:32,018
What is his displacement?

121
00:05:32,918 --> 00:05:33,818
Two.

122
00:05:33,382 --> 00:05:36,434
What does a minus sign in
a displacement tell you?

123
00:05:37,334 --> 00:05:38,234
Three.

124
00:05:37,957 --> 00:05:41,568
If you move the origin, does
the displacement change?

125
00:05:41,568 --> 00:05:42,468
Why?

126
00:05:43,188 --> 00:05:46,616
Next time: one lap of a
four hundred metre track.

127
00:05:46,616 --> 00:05:49,338
Distance four hundred, displacement zero.

128
00:05:49,338 --> 00:05:51,264
Can the two ever be equal?
